## Open questions for Will

These facts can only come from the host. Flag them in the MDX as `<!-- TODO: Will to confirm -->`.

1. **Jellyfish timing specificity.** What month does Will personally feel the jellyfish risk starts to thin out at the dock — late September? October? Has he ever had a jellyfish-free July? This is the one number readers want and only the host can give it honestly without overpromising.
2. **Mosquito mitigation at the property.** Does Will treat the yard? Are there fans on the screened porches? Citronella setup? This is relevant to whether the post should describe a mitigation or just name the screens.
3. **Tide offset from Point Lookout.** Does Will know roughly how many hours after Point Lookout high tide the water is high at the dock? Even a rough "about an hour later" from memory is useful.
4. **Low-salinity jellyfish observation.** Has Will personally noticed fewer jellyfish in wet years or after heavy rain? The science supports this but Will's firsthand observation would make it credible and specific.
5. **Specific "best month" Will would give a friend.** What month does he personally tell people to come if they want the full experience — water warm enough, jellyfish manageable, not peak-price August? His answer is the post's payoff line.
6. **Mosquito worst-week anecdote.** If Will has a specific story ("the week after a big storm in July…"), that is more useful than general guidance. Not required, but it would make the piece sing.

